IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`
IMPORT `aia-scope`
IMPORT `P3-section-3`

-- P3-art-23: Article 23 of the EU Artificial Intelligence Act (Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 as amended by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744): obligations of importers.
-- Lines 447-459 of the consolidated text. Unchanged by the Omnibus. Article 2(13) names Articles 9 to 15 and 17 to 25, so Article 23 is among those whose application may be limited for an Article 6(1) system (the gate).
-- The party is the importer (Art 3(6)); the keel decides who is one. The importer's seat asks the role once, in its own question.
-- Seams: Articles 11, 43 and 47 (what the importer has verified) and Article 79(1) (a risk) are plain BOOLEAN inputs named for the section they come from; PLAN.md section 4 lists none of them for this part (its S6 is asked by Articles 16 and 71); point (d) of paragraph 1 cites Article 22(1), which this part also encodes (P3-art-22).
-- Reading a result: JUST TRUE met; JUST FALSE the duty applies and is not met; NOTHING not covered (the group does not yet apply, Art 2(13) may limit the Article, or the paragraph's own trigger is absent).
-- For a bar ("shall not ... until"): JUST TRUE the bar is on, JUST FALSE it is off (the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, rules (b) and (d)).

DECLARE `Art 23 act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 23(1) verify, before placing the high-risk AI system on the market, the matters in points (a) to (d)`
    `Art 23(2) place the high-risk AI system on the market`
    `Art 23(2) inform the provider of the system, the authorised representative and the market surveillance authorities of the risk`
    `Art 23(3) indicate the importer's name, registered trade name or registered trade mark, and address`
    `Art 23(4) ensure that the storage or transport conditions do not jeopardise the compliance of the system with the requirements set out in Section 2`
    `Art 23(5) keep a copy of the certificate, the instructions for use and the EU declaration of conformity`
    `Art 23(5) cease to keep the copy of the certificate, the instructions for use and the EU declaration of conformity`
    `Art 23(6) provide the relevant competent authorities the necessary information and documentation`
    `Art 23(6) ensure that the technical documentation can be made available to the competent authorities`
    `Art 23(7) cooperate with the relevant competent authorities`

§ `Article 23(1): before placing, the importer verifies points (a) to (d)`

-- "shall ensure that the system is in conformity ... by verifying that": each point is a fact the importer has verified to be so; one that is not so, or was not verified, means the importer has not done what the paragraph says.
-- The deadline is the placement date in the `AI system` record, inclusive (fork F-prior-to in NOTES.md).
-- src:449 | 1. Before placing a high-risk AI system on the market, importers shall ensure that the system is in conformity with this Regulation by verifying that:
-- src:450 | (a) the relevant conformity assessment procedure referred to in Article 43 has been carried out by the provider of the high-risk AI system;
-- src:451 | (b) the provider has drawn up the technical documentation in accordance with Article 11 and Annex IV;
-- src:452 | (c) the system bears the required CE marking and is accompanied by the EU declaration of conformity referred to in Article 47 and instructions for use;
-- src:453 | (d) the provider has appointed an authorised representative in accordance with Article 22(1).
@ref Art 23(1) (src:449-453)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the importer has verified that the relevant conformity assessment procedure referred to in Article 43 has been carried out by the provider of the high-risk AI system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the importer has verified that the provider has drawn up the technical documentation in accordance with Article 11 and Annex IV` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the importer has verified that the system bears the required CE marking and is accompanied by the EU declaration of conformity referred to in Article 47 and instructions for use` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the importer has verified that the provider has appointed an authorised representative in accordance with Article 22(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 23(1) the importer has verified, before placing the system on the market, the matters in points (a) to (d)` MEANS
    CONSIDER gate
    WHEN `Section 3 applies` THEN
        IF `the importer has verified that the relevant conformity assessment procedure referred to in Article 43 has been carried out by the provider of the high-risk AI system` AND `the importer has verified that the provider has drawn up the technical documentation in accordance with Article 11 and Annex IV` AND `the importer has verified that the system bears the required CE marking and is accompanied by the EU declaration of conformity referred to in Article 47 and instructions for use` AND `the importer has verified that the provider has appointed an authorised representative in accordance with Article 22(1)`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Before placing a high-risk AI system on the market, importers shall ensure that the system is in conformity with this Regulation by verifying that"
    OTHERWISE `Section 3 the answer when the gate is shut` gate
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 23, "", 0)

@ref Art 23(1) (src:449-453)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 23 act`
`Art 23(1) the importer's duty to verify the matters in points (a) to (d) before placing the system on the market` MEANS
    IF `Section 3 the gate is open` gate
    THEN PARTY Importer
         MUST `Art 23(1) verify, before placing the high-risk AI system on the market, the matters in points (a) to (d)`
         WITHIN daysLeft
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY Importer BECAUSE "the matters in points (a) to (d) were not verified before the high-risk AI system was placed on the market"
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the gate is shut or Art 2(2) cuts the Article off
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 23, "", 0)
        placed MEANS `the AI system`'s `date placed on the market or put into service`
        daysLeft MEANS IF (Day placed) AT LEAST (Day `the date asked`) THEN (Day placed) MINUS (Day `the date asked`) ELSE 0


§ `Article 23(2): not placing the system on the market while the importer has sufficient reason to consider it non-conforming, falsified or accompanied by falsified documentation`

-- "it shall not place the system on the market until it has been brought into conformity": a bar. Before the system is brought into conformity the bar is on (JUST TRUE), after it is off (JUST FALSE; the "until" ruling of 2026-11-05, rule (d)).
-- Where the importer has no such reason the "Where" condition fails and the bar is off (JUST FALSE; the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, rule (b)): the function says that this paragraph does not bar the importer, not that the importer may place the system (fork F-when-upon in NOTES.md).
-- src:454 | 2. Where an importer has sufficient reason to consider that a high-risk AI system is not in conformity with this Regulation, or is falsified, or accompanied by falsified documentation, it shall not place the system on the market until it has been brought into conformity. Where the high-risk AI system presents a risk within the meaning of Article 79(1), the importer shall inform the provider of the system, the authorised representative and the market surveillance authorities to that effect.
@ref Art 23(2) first sentence (src:454)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the importer has sufficient reason to consider that the high-risk AI system is not in conformity with this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the importer has sufficient reason to consider that the high-risk AI system is falsified` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the importer has sufficient reason to consider that the high-risk AI system is accompanied by falsified documentation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the high-risk AI system has been brought into conformity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 23(2) the importer is barred from placing the high-risk AI system on the market` MEANS
    CONSIDER gate
    WHEN `Section 3 applies` THEN
        IF NOT (    `the importer has sufficient reason to consider that the high-risk AI system is not in conformity with this Regulation`
                 OR `the importer has sufficient reason to consider that the high-risk AI system is falsified`
                 OR `the importer has sufficient reason to consider that the high-risk AI system is accompanied by falsified documentation`)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an importer has sufficient reason to consider that a high-risk AI system is not in conformity with this Regulation, or is falsified, or accompanied by falsified documentation" (a "where" that fails: the periods ruling, rule (b))
        ELSE IF `the high-risk AI system has been brought into conformity`
             THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it shall not place the system on the market until it has been brought into conformity" (the "until" has been reached: ruling (d))
             ELSE JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE `Section 3 the answer when the gate is shut` gate
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 23, "", 0)

-- The same bar as a prohibition, for a trace: SHANT place the system on the market, from the date asked until the day before the system is brought into conformity.
-- With no date for the conformity (NOTHING) the bar has no end. Nothing is owed when the importer has no such reason or the gate is shut.
-- src:454 | 2. Where an importer has sufficient reason to consider that a high-risk AI system is not in conformity with this Regulation, or is falsified, or accompanied by falsified documentation, it shall not place the system on the market until it has been brought into conformity. Where the high-risk AI system presents a risk within the meaning of Article 79(1), the importer shall inform the provider of the system, the authorised representative and the market surveillance authorities to that effect.
@ref Art 23(2) first sentence (src:454)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the importer has sufficient reason to consider that the high-risk AI system is not in conformity with this Regulation, or is falsified, or accompanied by falsified documentation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the high-risk AI system is brought into conformity` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 23 act`
`Art 23(2) the importer's duty not to place the system on the market until it has been brought into conformity` MEANS
    IF `Section 3 the gate is open` gate AND `the importer has sufficient reason to consider that the high-risk AI system is not in conformity with this Regulation, or is falsified, or accompanied by falsified documentation`
    THEN CONSIDER `the date on which the high-risk AI system is brought into conformity`
         WHEN JUST conformityDate THEN
             IF (Day conformityDate) GREATER THAN (Day `the date asked`)
             THEN PARTY Importer
                  SHANT `Art 23(2) place the high-risk AI system on the market`
                  WITHIN ((Day conformityDate) MINUS (Day `the date asked`)) MINUS 1
                  HENCE FULFILLED
                  LEST BREACH BY Importer BECAUSE "the high-risk AI system was placed on the market before it had been brought into conformity"
             ELSE FULFILLED  -- the system is already in conformity on the date asked
         WHEN NOTHING THEN
             PARTY Importer
             SHANT `Art 23(2) place the high-risk AI system on the market`
             HENCE FULFILLED
             LEST BREACH BY Importer BECAUSE "the high-risk AI system was placed on the market before it had been brought into conformity"
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the gate is shut, Art 2(2) cuts the Article off, or the importer has no such reason
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 23, "", 0)

-- "Where the high-risk AI system presents a risk within the meaning of Article 79(1), the importer shall inform the provider of the system, the authorised representative and the market surveillance authorities to that effect."
-- src:454 | 2. Where an importer has sufficient reason to consider that a high-risk AI system is not in conformity with this Regulation, or is falsified, or accompanied by falsified documentation, it shall not place the system on the market until it has been brought into conformity. Where the high-risk AI system presents a risk within the meaning of Article 79(1), the importer shall inform the provider of the system, the authorised representative and the market surveillance authorities to that effect.
@ref Art 23(2) second sentence (src:454)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the high-risk AI system presents a risk within the meaning of Article 79(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the importer has informed the provider of the system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the importer has informed the authorised representative` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the importer has informed the market surveillance authorities` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 23(2) the importer has informed the provider, the authorised representative and the market surveillance authorities of the risk` MEANS
    CONSIDER gate
    WHEN `Section 3 applies` THEN
        IF NOT `the high-risk AI system presents a risk within the meaning of Article 79(1)`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where the high-risk AI system presents a risk within the meaning of Article 79(1), the importer shall inform" (no such risk)
        ELSE
             IF `the importer has informed the provider of the system` AND `the importer has informed the authorised representative` AND `the importer has informed the market surveillance authorities`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the importer shall inform the provider of the system, the authorised representative and the market surveillance authorities to that effect"
    OTHERWISE `Section 3 the answer when the gate is shut` gate
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 23, "", 0)

@ref Art 23(2) second sentence (src:454)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the high-risk AI system presents a risk within the meaning of Article 79(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 23 act`
`Art 23(2) the importer's duty to inform the provider, the authorised representative and the market surveillance authorities of the risk` MEANS
    IF `Section 3 the gate is open` gate AND `the high-risk AI system presents a risk within the meaning of Article 79(1)`
    THEN PARTY Importer
         MUST `Art 23(2) inform the provider of the system, the authorised representative and the market surveillance authorities of the risk`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY Importer BECAUSE "the provider, the authorised representative and the market surveillance authorities were not informed of the risk"
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the gate is shut, Art 2(2) cuts the Article off, or the system presents no risk within the meaning of Article 79(1)
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 23, "", 0)


§ `Article 23(3): the importer's name and address on the system and its packaging or documentation, where applicable`

-- "where applicable" qualifies the places of the indication (the system, its packaging, its accompanying documentation): the one input says that the indication is made at each place where it applies (fork F-23-3-places in NOTES.md).
-- src:455 | 3. Importers shall indicate their name, registered trade name or registered trade mark, and the address at which they can be contacted on the high-risk AI system and on its packaging or its accompanying documentation, where applicable.
@ref Art 23(3) (src:455)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the importer's name, registered trade name or registered trade mark is indicated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the address at which the importer can be contacted is indicated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the indications appear on the high-risk AI system and on its packaging or its accompanying documentation, where applicable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 23(3) the importer has indicated its name, registered trade name or registered trade mark, and its address` MEANS
    CONSIDER gate
    WHEN `Section 3 applies` THEN
        IF `the importer's name, registered trade name or registered trade mark is indicated` AND `the address at which the importer can be contacted is indicated` AND `the indications appear on the high-risk AI system and on its packaging or its accompanying documentation, where applicable`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Importers shall indicate their name, registered trade name or registered trade mark, and the address at which they can be contacted on the high-risk AI system and on its packaging or its accompanying documentation, where applicable"
    OTHERWISE `Section 3 the answer when the gate is shut` gate
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 23, "", 0)

@ref Art 23(3) (src:455)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 23 act`
`Art 23(3) the importer's duty to indicate its name, registered trade name or registered trade mark, and its address` MEANS
    IF `Section 3 the gate is open` gate
    THEN PARTY Importer
         MUST `Art 23(3) indicate the importer's name, registered trade name or registered trade mark, and address`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY Importer BECAUSE "the importer's name, registered trade name or registered trade mark and address were not indicated where applicable"
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the gate is shut or Art 2(2) cuts the Article off
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 23, "", 0)


§ `Article 23(4): storage and transport conditions while the system is under the importer's responsibility`

-- src:456 | 4. Importers shall ensure that, while a high-risk AI system is under their responsibility, storage or transport conditions, where applicable, do not jeopardise its compliance with the requirements set out in Section 2.
@ref Art 23(4) (src:456)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the high-risk AI system is under the importer's responsibility` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there are storage or transport conditions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the storage or transport conditions do not jeopardise the compliance of the system with the requirements set out in Section 2` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 23(4) the importer has ensured that the storage or transport conditions do not jeopardise the compliance of the system with Section 2` MEANS
    CONSIDER gate
    WHEN `Section 3 applies` THEN
        IF NOT `the high-risk AI system is under the importer's responsibility`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "while a high-risk AI system is under their responsibility" (the system is not under the importer's responsibility)
        ELSE
             IF NOT `there are storage or transport conditions`
             THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "storage or transport conditions, where applicable" (there are none)
             ELSE
                  IF `the storage or transport conditions do not jeopardise the compliance of the system with the requirements set out in Section 2`
                  THEN JUST TRUE
                  ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Importers shall ensure that, while a high-risk AI system is under their responsibility, storage or transport conditions, where applicable, do not jeopardise its compliance with the requirements set out in Section 2"
    OTHERWISE `Section 3 the answer when the gate is shut` gate
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 23, "", 0)

@ref Art 23(4) (src:456)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the high-risk AI system is under the importer's responsibility` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there are storage or transport conditions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 23 act`
`Art 23(4) the importer's duty to ensure that the storage or transport conditions do not jeopardise compliance with Section 2` MEANS
    IF `Section 3 the gate is open` gate AND `the high-risk AI system is under the importer's responsibility` AND `there are storage or transport conditions`
    THEN PARTY Importer
         MUST `Art 23(4) ensure that the storage or transport conditions do not jeopardise the compliance of the system with the requirements set out in Section 2`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY Importer BECAUSE "the storage or transport conditions jeopardised the compliance of the system with the requirements set out in Section 2"
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the gate is shut, Art 2(2) cuts the Article off, the system is not under the importer's responsibility, or there are no storage or transport conditions
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 23, "", 0)


§ `Article 23(5): keeping a copy of the certificate, the instructions for use and the EU declaration of conformity for 10 years`

-- Read as in Article 18(1): the last day of the period is the tenth anniversary of the placement (`add years`); the text gives no start, so the period runs from the placement (fork F-18-1 in NOTES.md).
-- src:457 | 5. Importers shall keep, for a period of 10 years after the high-risk AI system has been placed on the market or put into service, a copy of the certificate issued by the notified body, where applicable, of the instructions for use, and of the EU declaration of conformity referred to in Article 47.
@ref Art 23(5) (src:457)
GIVEN `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
GIVETH A DATE
`Art 23(5) the last day of the period for keeping the copies` MEANS
    `add years` (`the AI system`'s `date placed on the market or put into service`) 10

-- src:457 | 5. Importers shall keep, for a period of 10 years after the high-risk AI system has been placed on the market or put into service, a copy of the certificate issued by the notified body, where applicable, of the instructions for use, and of the EU declaration of conformity referred to in Article 47.
@ref Art 23(5) (src:457)
DECLARE `Art 23(5) what the importer keeps` HAS
    `there is a certificate issued by the notified body`           IS A BOOLEAN  -- "where applicable"
    `a copy of the certificate issued by the notified body`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `a copy of the instructions for use`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `a copy of the EU declaration of conformity referred to in Article 47` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:457 | 5. Importers shall keep, for a period of 10 years after the high-risk AI system has been placed on the market or put into service, a copy of the certificate issued by the notified body, where applicable, of the instructions for use, and of the EU declaration of conformity referred to in Article 47.
@ref Art 23(5) (src:457)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the copies` IS AN `Art 23(5) what the importer keeps`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 23(5) the importer keeps the copies for the period` MEANS
    CONSIDER gate
    WHEN `Section 3 applies` THEN
        IF (Day `the date asked`) LESS THAN (Day (`the AI system`'s `date placed on the market or put into service`))
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text names the end of the period, not its start (the date asked is before the placement; fork F-18-1)
        ELSE IF (Day `the date asked`) GREATER THAN (Day (`Art 23(5) the last day of the period for keeping the copies` `the AI system`))
             THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for a period of 10 years after the high-risk AI system has been placed on the market or put into service" (the period has ended: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, rule (a); fork F-18-1)
             ELSE IF       ((NOT `the copies`'s `there is a certificate issued by the notified body`) OR `the copies`'s `a copy of the certificate issued by the notified body`)
                          AND `the copies`'s `a copy of the instructions for use`
                          AND `the copies`'s `a copy of the EU declaration of conformity referred to in Article 47`
                     THEN JUST TRUE
                     ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Importers shall keep, for a period of 10 years after the high-risk AI system has been placed on the market or put into service, a copy of the certificate issued by the notified body, where applicable, of the instructions for use, and of the EU declaration of conformity referred to in Article 47"
    OTHERWISE `Section 3 the answer when the gate is shut` gate
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 23, "", 0)

-- src:457 | 5. Importers shall keep, for a period of 10 years after the high-risk AI system has been placed on the market or put into service, a copy of the certificate issued by the notified body, where applicable, of the instructions for use, and of the EU declaration of conformity referred to in Article 47.
@ref Art 23(5) (src:457)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 23 act`
`Art 23(5) the importer's duty to keep the copies for the period` MEANS
    IF `Section 3 the gate is open` gate
    THEN PARTY Importer
         SHANT `Art 23(5) cease to keep the copy of the certificate, the instructions for use and the EU declaration of conformity`
         WITHIN daysLeft
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY Importer BECAUSE "the copies were no longer kept before the end of the period of 10 years after the high-risk AI system was placed on the market or put into service"
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the gate is shut or Art 2(2) cuts the Article off
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 23, "", 0)
        lastDay MEANS `Art 23(5) the last day of the period for keeping the copies` `the AI system`
        daysLeft MEANS IF (Day lastDay) AT LEAST (Day `the date asked`) THEN (Day lastDay) MINUS (Day `the date asked`) ELSE 0

§ `Article 23(6): information and documentation upon a reasoned request, and making the technical documentation available`

-- src:458 | 6. Importers shall provide the relevant competent authorities, upon a reasoned request, with all the necessary information and documentation, including that referred to in paragraph 5, to demonstrate the conformity of a high-risk AI system with the requirements set out in Section 2 in a language which can be easily understood by them. For this purpose, they shall also ensure that the technical documentation can be made available to those authorities.
@ref Art 23(6) first sentence (src:458)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `a relevant competent authority has made a reasoned request to the importer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the importer has provided all the necessary information and documentation, including that referred to in paragraph 5, to demonstrate the conformity of the high-risk AI system with the requirements set out in Section 2` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information and documentation is in a language which can be easily understood by the authorities` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 23(6) the importer has provided the relevant competent authorities the necessary information and documentation upon a reasoned request` MEANS
    CONSIDER gate
    WHEN `Section 3 applies` THEN
        IF NOT `a relevant competent authority has made a reasoned request to the importer`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Importers shall provide the relevant competent authorities, upon a reasoned request, with all the necessary information and documentation" (no reasoned request has been made)
        ELSE
             IF `the importer has provided all the necessary information and documentation, including that referred to in paragraph 5, to demonstrate the conformity of the high-risk AI system with the requirements set out in Section 2` AND `the information and documentation is in a language which can be easily understood by the authorities`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Importers shall provide the relevant competent authorities, upon a reasoned request, with all the necessary information and documentation, including that referred to in paragraph 5, to demonstrate the conformity of a high-risk AI system with the requirements set out in Section 2 in a language which can be easily understood by them"
    OTHERWISE `Section 3 the answer when the gate is shut` gate
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 23, "", 0)

@ref Art 23(6) first sentence (src:458)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `a relevant competent authority has made a reasoned request to the importer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 23 act`
`Art 23(6) the importer's duty to provide the relevant competent authorities the necessary information and documentation upon a reasoned request` MEANS
    IF `Section 3 the gate is open` gate AND `a relevant competent authority has made a reasoned request to the importer`
    THEN PARTY Importer
         MUST `Art 23(6) provide the relevant competent authorities the necessary information and documentation`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY Importer BECAUSE "the necessary information and documentation were not provided to the relevant competent authorities"
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the gate is shut, Art 2(2) cuts the Article off, or no reasoned request has been made
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 23, "", 0)


-- src:458 | 6. Importers shall provide the relevant competent authorities, upon a reasoned request, with all the necessary information and documentation, including that referred to in paragraph 5, to demonstrate the conformity of a high-risk AI system with the requirements set out in Section 2 in a language which can be easily understood by them. For this purpose, they shall also ensure that the technical documentation can be made available to those authorities.
